{
  "_doc": "#1484 THE file-type to viewer/editor mapping, as data. `viewers[].id` names the lib that owns the file (wysiwyg = libs:wysiwyg, json = libs:json-viewer, media = libs:media-viewer, pdf = libs:pdf, odf = libs:odf); `formats` maps a format the viewer understands to the extensions that carry it. `modes` (View, Edit, Served) lists the modes a viewer offers, `format_modes` overrides it per format: for Markdown and HTML View is the rendered WYSIWYG view, editable; Edit is the raw source file; Served (HTML only) shows the page from a loopback-only local server (libs:local-serve) so relative CSS, JS and images resolve. A viewer with the single mode View is view only (media). `unsupported` is checked FIRST: the Microsoft Office formats are refused on purpose and answer `unsupported format`. A name no entry matches also answers unsupported. Adding a type or a mode is a data edit.",
